From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:08:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915: enable_dv_lab is a plain parameter, not an unsafe
 one

i915.enable_dv_lab (and xe.enable_dv_lab) turns the Dolby Vision tunnel of
Hades on HDMI on or off; it is on by default, and the documentation of the
build tells users to put enable_dv_lab=0 on the kernel line to turn native
Dolby Vision off on Intel graphics. The parameter was declared with
intel_display_param_named_unsafe(), so any value given to it on the kernel
line taints the kernel ("Setting dangerous option enable_dv_lab - tainting
kernel", TAINT_USER, param_check_unsafe() in kernel/params.c): the very
setting that the documentation recommends left a tainted kernel, which
makes later oops reports look like the user's own doing. Reported by YBLOD's
review of the build.

Nothing about the value is dangerous: 0 leaves the driver as it is without
the tunnel, and 1 is the default. It is now declared like the other
parameters of the tunnel (dv_pcon, hdmi_hdr_gmp), with intel_display_param_named(),
read-only in sysfs as before, and its description says what 0 does.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.c
index 44eb7cbc0..27138387a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.c
@@ -47,9 +47,16 @@ intel_display_param_named(hdmi_hdr_gmp, bool, 0400,
 	"HDR10 and HLG as later versions do (default: false). Not tried on a display: one that "
 	"does not take the packet from there shows HDR as a washed-out picture.");
 
-intel_display_param_named_unsafe(enable_dv_lab, bool, 0400,
-	"Experimental Standard-DV RGB8 tunnel, display9+ native HDMI (default: on). "
-	"Requires independently validated packed pixels and HDMI frame metadata.");
+/*
+ * Hades: a parameter like the others of the tunnel (dv_pcon, hdmi_hdr_gmp), not an unsafe one: an
+ * unsafe parameter taints the kernel whatever value it is given on the kernel line
+ * (param_check_unsafe()), and 0, the value that the documentation gives for turning the tunnel off,
+ * leaves the driver as it is without the tunnel.
+ */
+intel_display_param_named(enable_dv_lab, bool, 0400,
+	"The Dolby Vision tunnel of LibreELEC Hades on HDMI of display version 9 and later "
+	"(DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB and the properties beside it; default: on). "
+	"0 offers none of them: Dolby Vision plays as on a display without native output.");
 
 intel_display_param_named_unsafe(vbt_firmware, charp, 0400,
 	"Load VBT from specified file under /lib/firmware");
-- 
